BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:v16-0021@biotech-catalyst-calendar
DTSTAMP:20260924T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270228
SUMMARY:APMD — AD109 (aroxybutynin + atomoxetine) PDUFA decision
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DESCRIPTION:Indication: Obstructive sleep apnea\nThe FDA's decision date on AD109 (aroxybutynin + atomoxetine) for Obstructive sleep apnea falls on 2027-02-28 — the agency's yes-or-no moment for Apnimed\, Inc.'s application.\nNote: FDA accepted NDA for AD109 (aroxybutynin + atomoxetine) in obstructive sleep apnea (Phase 3 SynAIRgy and LunAIRo)\; PDUFA date February 28\, 2027. Apnimed completed an upsized IPO and began trading on the Nasdaq Global Select Market as APMD on 2026-07-31.\nDate quality: hard (2027-02-28)\nDetails: https://risdiplam.github.io/biotech-catalyst-calendar/#/event/v16-0021\nSource: https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/apnimed-announces-fda-acceptance-of-new-drug-application-for-ad109-an-investigational-oral-pill-to-treat-adults-with-obstructive-sleep-apnea-osa-302825008.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:v16-0023@biotech-catalyst-calendar
DTSTAMP:20260924T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270501
SUMMARY:AXSM — AXS-12 (reboxetine) PDUFA decision
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DESCRIPTION:Indication: cataplexy in narcolepsy\nNote: FDA accepted NDA\; PDUFA May 1\, 2027\; no AdCom planned. [Source verified 2026-09-20: 'The FDA has set a Prescription Drug User Fee Act (PDUFA) target action date of May 1\, 2027. The FDA also indicated that it does not currently plan to hold an advisory committee meeting to discuss the application.' (July]\nDate quality: hard (2027-05-01)\nDetails: https://risdiplam.github.io/biotech-catalyst-calendar/#/event/v16-0023\nSource: https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/07/15/3327580/33090/en/axsome-therapeutics-announces-fda-acceptance-of-new-drug-application-for-axs-12-for-the-treatment-of-cataplexy-in-narcolepsy.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
