DTSTAMP:20260924T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270508
SUMMARY:BBIO — encaleret PDUFA decision
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DESCRIPTION:Indication: autosomal dominant hypocalcemia type 1 (ADH1)\nNote: FDA accepted NDA\; PDUFA May 8\, 2027\; no AdCom planned\; no approved or advanced competitor in ADH1.\nDate quality: hard (2027-05-08)\nDetails: https://risdiplam.github.io/biotech-catalyst-calendar/#/event/v16-0046\nSource: https://investor.bridgebio.com/news/news-details/2026/BridgeBio-Announces-FDA-Acceptance-of-NDA-for-Encaleret-for-ADH1/default.aspx
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:v16-0062@biotech-catalyst-calendar
DTSTAMP:20260924T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270513
SUMMARY:BMY — mezigdomide PDUFA decision
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DESCRIPTION:Indication: relapsed/refractory multiple myeloma\nNote: FDA accepted NDA for mezigdomide (MeziKd: oral mezigdomide + carfilzomib + dexamethasone) in relapsed/refractory multiple myeloma\, based on Phase 3 SUCCESSOR-2 (NCT05552976\; PFS 18.0 vs 8.3 months\, HR 0.48\, p<0.0001). BMS PR 2026-07-13: 'The FDA has granted a Prescription Drug User Fee Act (PDUFA) date of May 13\, 2027 for this indication.' GAP: acceptance letter text not viewed\; acceptance confirm\nDate quality: hard (2027-05-13)\nDetails: https://risdiplam.github.io/biotech-catalyst-calendar/#/event/v16-0062\nSource: https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260713597234/en/U.S.-Food-and-Drug-Administration-Accepts-Bristol-Myers-Squibbs-New-Drug-Application-for-Mezigdomide-in-Patients-with-Relapsed-or-Refractory-Multiple-Myeloma
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:v16-0073@biotech-catalyst-calendar
DTSTAMP:20260924T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270121
SUMMARY:DYN — zeleciment rostudirsen (z-rostudirsen\, DYNE-251) PDUFA decision
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DESCRIPTION:Indication: Duchenne muscular dystrophy amenable to exon 51 skipping\nPhase 3 data for z-rostudirsen (DYNE-251) in Duchenne muscular dystrophy amenable to exon 51 skipping is expected on 2027-01-21 — the pivotal readout that determines whether Dyne Therapeutics\, Inc. can file for approval.\nNote: FDA accepted BLA and granted Priority Review\; exact PDUFA date disclosed in company PR.\nDate quality: hard (2027-01-21)\nDetails: https://risdiplam.github.io/biotech-catalyst-calendar/#/event/v16-0073\nSource: https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/07/20/3329635/0/en/Dyne-Therapeutics-Announces-U-S-FDA-Acceptance-of-Biologics-License-Application-BLA-for-Z-Rostudirsen-in-Exon-51-Duchenne-Muscular-Dystrophy-DMD.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:v16-0076@biotech-catalyst-calendar
DTSTAMP:20260924T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270629
SUMMARY:COGT — bezuclastinib PDUFA decision
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DESCRIPTION:Indication: advanced systemic mastocytosis (AdvSM)\nThe FDA's decision date on bezuclastinib for advanced systemic mastocytosis (AdvSM) falls on 2027-06-29 — the agency's yes-or-no moment for Cogent Biosciences\, Inc.'s application.\nNote: FDA accepted NDA and set PDUFA target action date 2027-06-29\; no AdCom planned at this time. NonAdvSM (2026-12-30) and GIST (2026-11-30) PDUFAs fall in 2026. [Source verified 2026-09-20: FDA has accepted its New Drug Application (NDA) for bezuclastinib in patients with Advanced Systemic Mastocytosis (AdvSM) and assigned a Prescription Drug User Fee Act (PDUFA) target action date of June 29\, 2027. \nDate quality: hard (2027-06-29)\nDetails: https://risdiplam.github.io/biotech-catalyst-calendar/#/event/v16-0076\nSource: https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/09/15/3361988/0/en/cogent-biosciences-announces-fda-acceptance-of-new-drug-application-nda-for-bezuclastinib-in-patients-with-advanced-systemic-mastocytosis-advsm.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:v16-0080@biotech-catalyst-calendar
DTSTAMP:20260924T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270227
SUMMARY:CGEM — zipalertinib PDUFA decision
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DESCRIPTION:Indication: locally advanced or metastatic NSCLC with EGFR exon 20 insertion mutations after platinum-based chemotherapy\nThe FDA's decision date on zipalertinib for locally advanced or metastatic NSCLC with EGFR exon 20 insertion mutations after platinum-based chemotherapy falls on 2027-02-27 — the agency's yes-or-no moment for Cullinan Therapeutics\, Inc.'s application.\nNote: FDA accepted NDA (post-platinum\, with or without prior amivantamab) with PDUFA 2027-02-27 per Cullinan/Taiho\; REZILIENT3 first-line Ph3 read out 2026\, not a 2027 event.\nDate quality: hard (2027-02-27)\nDetails: https://risdiplam.github.io/biotech-catalyst-calendar/#/event/v16-0080\nSource: https://www.taihooncology.com/us/news/us-food-and-drug-administration-accepts-new-drug-application-for-zipalertinib-for-the-treatment-of-locally-advanced-or-metastatic-non-small-cell-lung-cancer-with-egfr-exon-20-insertion-mutations/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
