STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DESCRIPTION:Indication: unresectable or metastatic conventional chondrosarcoma\nThe FDA's decision date on ozekibart (INBRX-109) for unresectable or metastatic conventional chondrosarcoma falls on 2027-04-14 — the agency's yes-or-no moment for Inhibrx Biosciences\, Inc.'s application.\nNote: FDA accepted BLA (no filing review issues)\; PDUFA goal April 14\, 2027. Would be first FDA-approved therapy for chondrosarcoma.\nDate quality: hard (2027-04-14)\nDetails: https://risdiplam.github.io/biotech-catalyst-calendar/#/event/v16-0116\nSource: https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/inhibrx-announces-us-fda-acceptance-of-bla-for-ozekibart-in-patients-with-conventional-chondrosarcoma-302800101.html
